<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaHead.xml                               Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-10
  ============================================================================

  THE PROBLEM (observed live 2026-08-10)
  ======================================
  Jawa spawned with random horns, slug-like eye-stalks and assorted alien
  skulls. Correct male-only, correct eye colours, wrong heads.

  ROOT CAUSE, AND IT IS NOT WHAT IT LOOKS LIKE
  ============================================
  This is NOT caused by removing Outland_GreaterGoblinoidHead. Removing that
  gene removed a CONSTRAINT that was hiding a pre-existing problem.

  The load set contains 318 HeadTypeDefs, and 206 of them declare NO
  requiredGenes at all, which means they are eligible for ANY pawn that has no
  forced head. Worst contributors: Alpha Genes 56, Star Wars Xenotypes 41,
  Outer Rim Galactic Diversity 40, Outland Genetics 16. So a pawn with no head
  gene rolls from a pool two thirds of which is modded alien skulls.

  Every FA-drawn pawn in the colony has been rolling those heads all along.
  Facial Animation simply paints over the head node, so nobody ever saw it.
  Excluding the Jawa from FA is what made the underlying pollution visible.

  THE FIX
  =======
  Give the Jawa an explicit head gene that forces vanilla human heads. A plain
  head under the hood with two glowing eyes on it is the canonical Jawa read
  anyway: the face is never seen.

  Both genders are listed even though Jawa are currently male-only via
  Outland_AllMale, so this still behaves if that decision is ever reversed.

  Deliberately NOT fixing the 206 ungated head types globally. That would be a
  large behavioural change to every pawn in a 562-mod stack, and for everyone
  except the FA-excluded xenotypes it is invisible. Scoped to the Jawa on
  purpose; the global issue is recorded in benign_log_errors.md instead.

  ALTERNATIVES if a plain head reads as too plain: swap this gene on the
  xenotype for Outland_RattyHead or Outland_LesserGoblinoidHead, both of which
  suit a small hooded scavenger. Those carry their own baked-in facial art
  though, which is exactly what produced the fangs-and-spider-eyes problem the
  goblinoid head gave us.

  HOOD IS NOW PART OF THE HEAD, NOT JUST APPAREL  [added 2026-09-25]
  ====================================================================
  Owner, verbatim: "we need urgently to ensure that Jawa swimming maintain
  their hoods. Jawa should never be seen without a hood. It's unholy." Scope
  widened same day to EVERY render path, not just swimming.

  A Harmony fix on the swimming render-flags path (Verse.PawnRenderer.
  ParallelGetPreRenderResults clears PawnRenderFlags.Headgear/.Clothes while
  swimming) would only have covered swimming. Sleeping, lovin', the styling
  station and a genuinely stripped/naked Jawa don't clear those flags at all —
  they just have no apparel drawn, and the owner's ruling is that the hood is
  not optional apparel, it is part of what a Jawa IS. So the hood is now a
  render node on THIS gene, added by JawaRules/Patches/RSW_JawaHood.xml so this def never names a
  type from an assembly that may be absent (a missing workerClass discards the whole gene), parented to the Head
  tag, reusing guy762_JawaHood's own worn texture
  (SWApparel/Robes/jawa/hood[_north/_south/_east], Armoury mod).

  MEASURED (RimSage, Verse/PawnRenderNode.cs, PawnRenderNodeWorker.cs,
  PawnRenderNodeWorker_Head.cs): a node's own CanDrawNow is the only per-node
  gate PawnRenderNode.AppendRequests checks, and the default
  PawnRenderNodeWorker.CanDrawNow never reads PawnRenderFlags.Headgear,
  .Clothes, .Invisible or .Portrait — those are apparel-node-specific checks
  (PawnRenderNodeWorker_Apparel_Head). PawnRenderNodeWorker_Head adds exactly
  one extra gate, HeadStump (a decapitated pawn correctly shows no hood — there
  is no head to hood). So this node draws under swimming (and inherits the
  Head node's own -0.5 swimming offset for free), sleeping, lovin', the
  styling station, stripped/naked, portraits, the colonist bar, and corpses
  (rotDrawMode below includes Rotting).

  The worker class (RimMandrake.StarWars.JawaRules.
  PawnRenderNodeWorker_JawaHoodFallback, in the JawaRules assembly — no new
  DLL needed) skips drawing this node when guy762_JawaHood is actually
  equipped AND its own flags allow it to render, so the real (dyeable) apparel
  item draws instead of a static duplicate underneath it. Every other case —
  hood not equipped, or equipped but flag-suppressed — draws this fallback,
  which is why a Jawa is never bare-headed even with the coat off.

  MINIMAL BY DESIGN, NOT LAYER-MATCHED TO THE REAL HOOD  [revised 2026-09-25]
  ============================================================================
  Owner, same sitting: keep this fallback SMALLER than a real hood and drawn
  BEHIND normal headgear, so any player-chosen hat still shows in front and
  obscures it — protection against a bare head, not a fashion lock-in.

  drawSize 0.75 (real apparel draws at the default 1.0) and baseLayer 65 —
  above Head/Beard/Hair (50/60/62, Defs/Core/PawnRenderTreeDefs/
  PawnRenderTreeDefs.xml) so it still reads as a hood covering the head, but
  BELOW the Overhead apparel layer real headgear renders at (guy762_JawaHood
  itself: 71 default / 90 north) so any worn hat — the real Jawa hood or any
  other headgear — draws on top and hides this smaller fallback entirely.
  RimWorld's render-layer numbering is shared across the whole tree, not
  head-local, which is what makes "below every hat, above bare skin" a
  single flat number rather than a per-rotation table.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GeneDef>
    <defName>RSW_Jawa_Head_Plain</defName>
    <label>hooded face</label>
    <labelShortAdj>hooded</labelShortAdj>
    <description>Carriers of this gene have an unremarkable head, which is just as well: nobody has ever seen one. Beneath the hood there is only the glow of two enormous eyes.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_Hair</iconPath>
    <displayOrderInCategory>1780</displayOrderInCategory>
    <biostatCpx>0</biostatCpx>
    <forcedHeadTypes>
      <li>Male_AverageNormal</li>
      <li>Male_AverageWide</li>
      <li>Male_NarrowNormal</li>
      <li>Male_NarrowPointy</li>
      <li>Female_AverageNormal</li>
      <li>Female_NarrowNormal</li>
    </forcedHeadTypes>
  </GeneDef>

</Defs>
